From: Mohammed <91819504+mohammed7s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:04:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] cur: include the Computer Control consent app

Set RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL so that build/make adds the
VirtualDeviceManager package (frameworks/base/packages/VirtualDeviceManager)
to the product. It holds the system dialog in which the user approves an
agent's request to automate an app. Without it, a session request that
needs consent has nowhere to send the user and can never be approved.

The dialog filters touches when obscured and hides non-system overlays,
and it runs on the default display, where a Computer Control session
cannot inject input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flag_values/cur/RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL.textproto | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 flag_values/cur/RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL.textproto

diff --git a/flag_values/cur/RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL.textproto b/flag_values/cur/RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL.textproto
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aac340e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/flag_values/cur/RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL.textproto
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+name: "RELEASE_PACKAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL"
+value: {
+  bool_value: true
+}
